2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] Common ways it could have been installed on Arch:
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] - venv + pip – `python -m venv env1 && source env1/bin/activate && pip install ultralytics`
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] → `env1/bin/yolo`
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] - pip --user – `pip install --user ultralytics` → `~/.local/bin/yolo`
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] - pipx – `pipx install ultralytics` → `~/.local/bin/yolo`
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] - system pip – `sudo pip install ultralytics` → `/usr/local/bin/yolo`
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] - AUR – `yay -S python-ultralytics` → `/usr/bin/yolo`
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] - conda/mamba – `conda install -c conda-forge ultralytics` → `$CONDA_PREFIX/bin/yolo`
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] - uv tool – `uv tool install ultralytics` → `~/.local/bin/yolo`
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] If you created the venv with `--system-site-packages`, it can import system packages, but the
2026-10-01 22:23:32 [deepseek-flash] `yolo` script stays in `/usr/bin`. That would still be found if `/usr/bin` is on `PATH`.
