2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.001 34.95KB 2.54s
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] Yes. In nano:
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] • Ctrl + \\* (that’s `Ctrl` + backslash) opens “Search (to replace)”.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 1. Type the text to find, press Enter.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 2. Type the replacement, press Enter.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 3. Nano asks `Replace this instance?` — press A to replace All.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash]    - `Y` replaces just this one.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash]    - `N` skips to the next.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash]    - `Ctrl + C` cancels.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] Notes:
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] - It’s literal text matching by default, not regex. No `\n` or `.*`.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] - It searches from the cursor position forward, then wraps around, so it covers the whole file
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] either way.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] - If `Ctrl + \` doesn’t reach nano (some terminals grab it), use Alt + R as the alternative
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] binding, or `Esc` then `R`.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] - Undo is Alt + U (or `Esc` then `U`) if you get it wrong. Redo is Alt + E.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] - Check nano’s bottom bar — it lists `^R Replace` when a replace prompt is active, and the version
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] number tells you if you have an old build. `nano --version`.
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] If your replacement needs patterns (regex, column reordering, only lines starting with X), nano
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] isn’t the right tool — use `sed` or a small Python script instead, and I can write that for you if
2026-10-01 22:33:24 [deepseek-flash] you paste the `ak1.txt` format.
