2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] Likely causes, in order of probability:
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] 1. `run.sh` points at a directory with no images. The previous run pointed at a hardcoded
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] path that didn’t exist; you probably edited it to something else that’s also wrong — an empty dir,
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] or `runs/`, or `content/`.
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] 2. `run.sh` points at `ak1.txt` thinking Ultralytics will parse it. Ultralytics treats a
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] `.txt` source as a list of image paths, one per line. If `ak1.txt` holds annotations
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] (`class x1 y1 x2 y2 …`), none of those lines are valid files and the loader ends up with nothing
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] usable.
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] 3. Shell glob that expanded to nothing. If `run.sh` has `source=/some/dir/.jpg` and no
2026-10-01 22:35:48 [deepseek-flash] jpgs match, bash passes the literal `.jpg` through.
