2026-10-05 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.016 1.373MB 31.58s
2026-10-05 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] The script is a faithful generator for the `godot.json` we looked at, with a couple of divergences
2026-10-05 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] and a few small things worth flagging.
2026-10-05 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-05 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] It reproduces the earlier file closely
2026-10-05 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-05 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] - `variant` list, `globals`, category ordering, tab-indented JSON, and the `is_parent_class`
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] semantics all match the observed output. In particular, `ClassDB.is_parent_class` returns true when
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] the two names are equal, which is why `Node`, `Resource`, and `Object` appear in their own category
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] lists — that is intentional, not an accident of the loop.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - `get_variant_names` produces the same sorted list (including `Variant` inserted via the guard, so
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] no duplicate from `type_string`).
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - `is_editor_class` covers every entry in the earlier `editor` array: all of them begin with
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] `Editor` or `ResourceImporter`.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] Where it diverges from the earlier JSON
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - The earlier file has `"version": "0.2.0"` and a `"guide"` section describing `Node` and `Node2D`.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] The script emits `"version": "0.1.0"` and no `guide`. So either the earlier file was hand-edited,
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] or a newer revision of this script exists.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - The earlier `"curator"` is `"Curated by nitrologic"`; the script emits `"nitrologic"`. Cosmetic,
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] but worth aligning.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] Small points
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - The triple-quoted string after `extends SceneTree` is not a docstring — GDScript has no docstring
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] mechanism, and a bare string at script scope is an unused expression (warning, not error).
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] Idiomatic GDScript documentation uses `##` line comments. If the intent is documentation, that is
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] the cleaner choice.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - `str(registered_class)` is redundant: `ClassDB.get_class_list()` already returns a
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] `PackedStringArray` of `String`. Harmless, but it hides the type.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - `ClassDB.get_class_list()` only includes editor-registered classes when the editor-enabled binary
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] is used. Running this via the non-editor template (or a stripped export) will silently drop the
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] whole `editor` array rather than error. Worth an explicit assertion or a printed warning if
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] `editors.is_empty()`.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - `is_editor_class` is a name-prefix heuristic. It happens to match the current class list, but any
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] future editor class not prefixed `Editor`/`ResourceImporter` (and there is no public `ClassDB`
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] query for "editor-only") will be missed. A short comment noting the heuristic would help a future
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] reader.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - `Engine.get_version_info().string` would give the same `major.minor.patch` string; the manual
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] formatting is fine, but the dict field already exists.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] - `_init` on a `SceneTree` script does work for `--script` invocation because the script instance
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] is constructed before the main loop starts; `quit()` then takes effect on the first iteration. If
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] you ever move to `extends MainLoop`, the virtual to override is `_initialize`/`_process`, not
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] `_init`.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] Suggestion
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] If you want the script to emit the `0.2.0` shape, the changes are: bump the literal version, add a
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] static `guide` dictionary, and set `curator` to the descriptive string. All three are plain
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] dictionary edits in `build_schema_dictionary`. Say the word and I can draft them.
2026-10-05 13:04:31 [deepseek-flash] 
