2026-10-16 14:44:42 [gemini-4-argon] typing `echo`, followed by a space, and then `$VARIABLE_NAME` (keeping in mind that environment
2026-10-16 14:44:42 [gemini-4-argon] variables are case-sensitive and typically written in uppercase).
2026-10-16 14:44:42 [gemini-4-argon] 
2026-10-16 14:44:42 [gemini-4-argon] Alternatively, you can also use the `printenv` utility followed by the variable name, which does
2026-10-16 14:44:42 [gemini-4-argon] not require the dollar sign prefix.
