2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] Thanks for sharing. I don't have an earlier version of these files in our conversation to diff
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] against, so I've treated this as a fresh read of `wire.js` and `isowire.html`. A few observations,
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] starting with things that look like genuine bugs:
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] • Likely runtime breakers*
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - In `World.addPanel`, the bare assignment to `parent` collides with the read-only `window.parent`.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] In sloppy mode the assignment is silently ignored, so the subsequent `getElementsByTagName` call on
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] it would throw. This one is worth renaming to a declared local.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - In the viewport loop inside `Panel.draw`, the call to `this.drawLayers` only passes `trans` and
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] `screen` — the `layers` and `drawlist` parameters arrive undefined and the iteration throws. It's
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] latent for now since no elements in the current HTML carry a `viewport` attribute.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `Panel.populate` runs unconditionally after construction, but when `WireContext` fails to get a
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] GL context the constructor returns early with `this.context` unset, so populate will throw on the
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] missing context.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `Layer.setShorts` references a bare `gl` instead of `this.gl` — a ReferenceError if it's ever
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] called (currently unused, but a trap).
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - In `pollMidi`, iterating a `MIDIInput` object directly with `for...of` will throw, since those
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] aren't iterable — the loop structure looks like it was written for an older map-of-maps API.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] • Correctness issues*
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - In `Panel.drawLayers`, `this.check;` appears four times without parentheses, so the GL error
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] check never actually runs.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `Panel.addLineShapes` binds attributes against `this.lineLayer` but adds the shape to
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] `this.flatLayer` — the line geometry ends up drawn through the triangle program. Possibly
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] intentional, but it reads like a mismatch.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - The `clear` attribute colour parsing in `Viewport.set` both shifts incorrectly for a six-digit
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] hex value and passes raw 0–255 components to `gl.clearColor`, which expects 0.0–1.0.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `Viewport.set` scales by `window.devicePixelRatio` while `resizeCanvas` hardcodes its multiplier
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] to 1.0 — on HiDPI displays the scissor/viewport rectangles won't match the backing store.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] Relatedly, the GL viewport Y coordinate is the bottom-left corner; the current expression doesn't
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] subtract the element height.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `pointLayer` is tagged with both `depthEnable` and `depthDisable`, so it's included in both
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] passes of `drawLayerList` and points get drawn twice per frame.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `MidiInterface` assignment in `yesMidi` calls `onMidiState()` immediately and assigns its return
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] value rather than the function reference.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `onRun` re-invokes `onLoad`, which re-attaches the body event listeners and starts additional
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] `requestAnimationFrame`/`setTimeout` loops each time — the render loops accumulate, and old GL
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] contexts are never released.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] • Smaller items*
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `Player.thurst` is presumably meant to be "thrust", and `turn(player, steps)` ignores its
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] `player` argument in favour of `playerFocus`.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `Segments.swizzle` references `segs` rather than `this.segs` in one spot.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - Several implicit globals: `iii` in `skimpPoly`, `i` in `addWall`, `v` in `Surface.drill`, `line`
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] in `shaderError`, `midiIn`/`midiOut` in `pollMidi`, `buffer` in `noiseBuffer`, and `area` in
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] `onHide`/`onShow`.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - In `IncittiFont` the `','` key is defined twice (the second wins), and there's an empty-string
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] key that looks like a lost `'{'` glyph.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `failVR`, `enableVR` and `enableXRDevice` all reference `vr`, which only exists in the
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] commented-out code in `onLoad` — they'd throw if ever invoked. Same story for `context`,
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] `dogBarkingBuffer` and `onError` in `loadWav`, which reads like pasted sample code.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `Shape.position` contains a no-op `if(bucket){ bucket; }`, `Viewport.setBounds` computes
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] `moved`/`sized` without using them, and the `edges` dictionary built in `Surface.bevil` is never
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] read.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `onKeyDown` doesn't filter by target, so typing `a` or `d` in the shader textareas also rotates
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] the view.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] - `onFullscreen` only uses the `webkitRequestFullScreen` path; the standard `requestFullscreen`
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] would be a safer fallback.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] • Things I rather liked*
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] The instancing design is tidy — per-bucket `handles` uniforms reset before each instanced draw,
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] with `gl_InstanceID` restarting per bucket so indexing stays correct. The retained command list in
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] `Shape.add` executed via `apply` is a nice pattern, the `norm`-prefix convention for normalised
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] int16 attributes is doing real work, and putting the shaders in editable textareas with F6 to
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] re-run makes for a pleasant live-tweak workflow. The isometric projection done directly in the
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] vertex shaders keeps the CPU-side matrix minimal.
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] Happy to go deeper on any of these, or to write up concrete fixes in code form if you'd like — just
2026-10-16 15:07:45 [glm-5.3] say which ones.
