2026-10-23 19:38:21 [glm-5.3] • Concrete improvements*
2026-10-23 19:38:21 [glm-5.3] 
2026-10-23 19:38:21 [glm-5.3] 1. Inject runtime identity. If your harness knows the account, provider, and model string
2026-10-23 19:38:21 [glm-5.3] for each request, template them into the system prompt per-call. Then the model isn't guessing —
2026-10-23 19:38:21 [glm-5.3] it's reading. Something like "You are served via {account} / {model} on this request." This is the
2026-10-23 19:38:21 [glm-5.3] only approach that makes self-reports trustworthy, because the model's knowledge comes from your
2026-10-23 19:38:21 [glm-5.3] ground truth, not its weights.
