2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.6 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.031 287.0KB 125.95s
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] Reviewed the new `relay.ts`, `relaybot.ts`, `slopprompt.ts`, `slopsearch.ts` and `client.ts`, plus
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] the `forge.md` edit. Comments on what changed, then the defects that stand out.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] Documentation
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `/files` now says `forge.log` instead of `history.log` — that resolves the naming conflict I
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] flagged last time, but the `/share` section below it still points at `"agents.md", "history.log"
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] and "relay.md"`, so the stale name survives in the one place a reader is sent to look. `agents.md`
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] is still undocumented.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] More significant: several documented commands have no handler in `callCommand` at all.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] - `/project [drop] [key]` and config flag 20 `project` — no `case "project"`. The
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `keyedShares`/`setProject` machinery is commented out in `addShare` and `commitShares`, so the
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] README claim that "/share of a relay.md keys a project to that folder name" describes behaviour
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] that isn't in this build. The transcript in the earlier share (`[KEY] loadProject elfutil`) is from
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 1.9.x.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] - `/files` — documented, no handler.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] - `/history` and `/list` are presented as synonyms for a conversation summary, but `list` calls
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `listHistory` and `history` calls `readHistory`, which parses log files and reports per-day tag
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] byte counts. Very different commands.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] Conversely `persona`, `tex`, `spec`, `sys` and `announce` are implemented and undocumented.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `/think` documents a 0–8192 budget, but `grokThink` is only emitted when `info.pricing.length > 3`,
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] which reads as a proxy for "supports thinking" — so `/think` is silently inert for most models.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `/say` is documented as taking "previous or specified text" but ignores its arguments. `/drop`
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] still says "drop all files" while the implementation is per-index.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] Config descriptions have also drifted: flag 3 is "enable model websearch tool interface" in
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `forge.md` and "enable search tool interface" in `flagNames`; flag 13 differs similarly. And
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `relayVersion` is now `2.0.6` while the README badge says `2.0.5`.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] Configuration defaults are not merged
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `readForge` replaces `roha.config` wholesale with the parsed JSON. Any flag absent from an existing
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `forge.json` is `undefined`, not the `emptyConfig` default. That is not cosmetic: `syncRelay`
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] defaults true but resolves falsy, so an older forge silently takes the `else` branch into
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `beginRelay` — the WIP async path that pushes a literal `"completion ready"` into history. Same for
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `thinking`, `listen` and `project`. `emptyConfig` also omits `search` and `persona` entirely, so
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] their documented defaults never apply even on a fresh forge.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] Related: `ConfigFlags` declares `persona: string`, but it is toggled as a boolean by `/config` and
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] tested as a boolean in the `responses` path. And `budget` is typed as the literal `false`, so
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] assigning `true` is a type error.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] Persistence
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `writeForge` builds `json` and then assigns `roha.model = grokModel` before writing `json` — the
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] assignment happens after serialisation, so the selected model is never actually saved. The next
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] boot falls back to `defaultModel`.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] Bugs with immediate consequences
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] - `announceCommand` iterates `for (const connection of slopConnections)` on a `Map`, so
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `connection` is a `[key, value]` pair; `connection?.write` is undefined and the call throws. It
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] needs `.values()`.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] - `open(...)` is called in `geminiSay`, `gptSay` and the speech branch of `relay`, but nothing
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] named `open` is imported or defined — only `openCommand` and `openWithDefaultApp` exist. Those
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] three TTS paths should throw `ReferenceError`.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] - `geminiToolCalls` emits `{thought_signature, function_call:{name, args}}` and assigns that to
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `message.tool_calls`, but `relay` and `processToolCalls` both expect `{id, type, function:{name,
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] arguments}}`. `tool.function.name` will throw on the first Gemini function call. The commented-out
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] `oldGeminiToolCalls` produces the correct shape.
2026-10-24 08:23:29 [deepseek-flash] - `anthropicMessages` switches on `user` and `assistant` only — there is no `tool` case, so tool
