2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] - `squashMessages` mutates live history. It pushes the original item references into
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] `squashed` and then does `last.content += "\n" + current.content`. `/log` calls it with
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] `rohaHistory` directly when `config.squash` is set, so a single `/log` permanently concatenates
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] entries in the real history. It needs shallow copies per item.
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] - `slopFrames` is undeclared. The slops worker handler calls
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] `slopFrames.push(payload.frame)` on a `tick` event, but no `slopFrames` is declared anywhere.
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] Latent only because `config.slops` defaults false, but it will throw on the first frame when
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] enabled.
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] - `MaxFileSize` can never be sent. It evaluates to exactly 16777216 (16 MiB), which equals
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] Kimi's total-message cap quoted in your notes. Base64 alone is ~22.4 MB for a file at that limit,
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] before blob metadata and history. A per-file cap of roughly 11 MB, or a check on the encoded
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] request size, would prevent the guaranteed failure.
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] - `geminiSay` hardcodes the account key `rohaEndpoint["gemini"]`. Every other provider
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] lookup derives the key from the model name. If the account is named `google` in `accounts.json`,
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] `/say` throws on a missing endpoint rather than reporting a configuration error.
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] - Unawaited `resetModel` at startup. The module-level call is not awaited, so its internal
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] `writeForge` from `aboutModel` races the later `writeForge` calls in the boot sequence.
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] - `keyedShares` is now dead state that survives in `emptyRoha`, `readForge`, `resetCommand`
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] and the commented-out lines in `addShare`/`commitShares`, so it will keep being serialised into
2026-10-24 08:34:42 [deepseek-flash] `forge.json`. `shareName()` is likewise unused now that the `setProject` call is commented out.
